From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 12:56:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] libcamera: software_isp: Support unpacked 14-bit Bayer

MediaTek's CAMSV writes unpacked RAW10 shifted into 14 bits per 16-bit
word, so a sensor behind it can only be described as 14-bit Bayer. Add
the unpacked 14-bit formats to the CPU debayer, the CPU statistics and
the GPU debayer, scaling by 64 to 8 bits as the 10- and 12-bit paths
scale by 4 and 16.

Tested on a Zinwa Q25 (MT6789, IMX111): 1600x1200 at 30 fps on both
the CPU and the GPU path.
---
 .../internal/software_isp/swstats_cpu.h       |  1 +
 src/libcamera/shaders/bayer_unpacked.frag     |  3 ++
 src/libcamera/software_isp/debayer_cpu.cpp    | 33 +++++++++++++++++--
 src/libcamera/software_isp/debayer_cpu.h      |  5 +++
 src/libcamera/software_isp/debayer_egl.cpp    | 24 ++++++++++++++
 src/libcamera/software_isp/swstats_cpu.cpp    | 30 +++++++++++++++++
 6 files changed, 94 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

